    "result": "I implemented both functions in `solution.py` and wrote 30 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 30. `can_book` checks the rules in the spec's order: it raises `ValueError` for a non-positive duration or negative buffer, then returns `False` for a cross-day booking, a duration over 4 hours, or a start/end outside open/close. For conflicts it allows a booking only if it starts at or after `existing_end + buffer` or ends at or before `existing_start - buffer`, which gives half-open and back-to-back behaviour at buffer 0. `merge_intervals` validates every interval first, then sorts a copy by start and merges any interval that starts at or before the current merged end, so touching intervals join; the input list is not modified. I did not run a coverage measurement, since the coverage tool was not part of the allowed commands. The tests exercise every branch in both functions, so I expect coverage above the 90% gate, but that is unverified.",
